1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,920
Where Spider-Man’s web attaches

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:06,240
changes the depth and path of the swing.

3
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:07,340
Yet the player

4
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:09,780
does not aim at a building point every time.

5
00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:11,660
The developers take the intended travel direction

6
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:14,200
and choose a suitable attachment point.

7
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:15,460
An early approach cast multiple lines

8
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:17,340
to find places where they meet buildings.

9
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:19,580
This kind of test is called a raycast.

10
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:21,020
But between those test lines,

11
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:24,480
thin structures and corners could be missed.

12
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:27,400
Adding more rays alone was not a convenient fix.

13
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:30,940
Buildings were marked with simple box volumes.

14
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:32,360
Choosing candidates on continuous faces

15
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:35,080
helps reduce the gaps between test lines.

16
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:38,440
Production tools automate marking the large city.

17
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:41,400
Finally, check whether the result touches real geometry.

18
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:43,360
Next, construct an ideal reference.

19
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:46,620
Use stick direction, desired rope length and slope

20
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:48,980
to identify a good starting position.

21
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:52,780
Combine a nearby point on the building with one toward travel.

22
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:55,720
Adjust candidates that would let the player fall too deeply.

23
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:56,580
When there are several candidates,

24
00:00:56,580 --> 00:01:00,480
score factors such as direction, distance and slope.

25
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:02,800
Choose a well-scoring attachment point.

26
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:05,400
Avoid forcing a connection to a poor location.

27
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:08,180
Debug views of selected points and movement history

28
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:09,640
helped the developers tune the behavior.

29
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:12,820
Once the web is taut, consider gravity and its direction.

30
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:16,400
A good anchor lets you travel in the intended direction.

31
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:19,320
The game chooses the attachment so we can focus on moving.
